# AI Library Entry Governance

Use `ai-library-entry` as the primary kickoff whenever the task adds or
materially refreshes durable content under `ai-resource-library/`.

This rule applies to work targeting:

- `vendors/`
- `sdk-context/`
- `indexes/`
- `prompts/`

## Required behavior

1. Classify the requested work into one or more content families:
   - `vendor_docs`
   - `sdk_api_context`
   - `library_indexes`
   - `operator_prompts`
2. Create a governed packet under `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD--slug/README.md`
   before major collection or synthesis work.
3. Create a packet-local `entry-spec.yml` before collection/build work that
   declares sources, outputs, modes, routing, Context7 expectations, asset
   requirements, and validation rules.
4. Use Firecrawl first for live vendor/product/help docs; use Playwright when
   JS/login/browser state is needed; use Fetch only as a lightweight fallback.
5. Use Context7 proactively for implementation syntax, version-pinned library
   resolution, topic-sharded SDK notes, **OpenAPI/Swagger interpretation**,
   page-coverage validation, **Firecrawl cross-checks**, and `library_indexes`
   packs under `indexes/<entry>/`.
6. When `vendor_docs` and `context7_required` are both true, also produce
   `indexes/<entry>/` (README, crosswalk, Firecrawl↔Context7 cross-check) and
   update those indexes when adding new pages or API surfaces.
7. Use `vendor-doc-collection` only as the narrower helper when the routed
   output needs a structured vendor-doc export tree.
8. Do not mark the entry complete until:
   - `library-entry-validate` passes for `entry-spec.yml`
   - required outputs exist in their declared target roots
   - required provenance and asset declarations are satisfied
   - Firecrawl↔Context7 cross-check artifacts exist when both tools are in scope

## Skill family delegation

After packet + `entry-spec.yml` exist, delegate per `references/skill-family-map.md`:

- `library-entry-build` — registered build scripts
- `library-context7-pack` — Context7 shards
- `firecrawl-context7-crosscheck` — gap JSON
- `library-indexes-pack` — indexes routing pack
- `library-entry-validate` — completion gate

## Boundary

This rule does not force all ai-library work into `vendors/`.
Routing is part of the capability.

This rule also does not convert ordinary research notes into a durable entry.
It applies when the task is actually building or materially refreshing durable
library content.
